# SIEM Deployment Evidence

## Overview

This section contains evidence of the deployment and configuration of the Wazuh Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) environment used for this project.

## Objective

The objective of this phase was to establish a centralized security monitoring platform capable of receiving, processing, and analyzing security telemetry from multiple endpoints.

## Environment

The SOC lab included:

- Wazuh SIEM
- Wazuh Manager
- Wazuh Dashboard
- Wazuh Indexer
- Debian Linux
- Windows Server 2025
- Kali Linux
- Wazuh endpoint agents
- Virtualized lab networking

## Deployment

Wazuh was deployed as the primary SIEM platform.

The deployment provided the central infrastructure required for:

- Endpoint monitoring
- Log ingestion
- Security-event analysis
- Threat detection
- Alert generation
- Threat hunting
- Incident investigation

Wazuh agents were configured on monitored endpoints to forward security telemetry to the Wazuh Manager.

## Validation

Deployment validation included confirming:

- Wazuh services were operational
- The Wazuh Dashboard was accessible
- Endpoint agents were registered
- Agents were communicating with the manager
- Security events were visible within Wazuh

## Evidence

The accompanying evidence PDF contains screenshots demonstrating the SIEM deployment, configuration, agent connectivity, and operational Wazuh environment.

## Outcome

A functioning centralized SIEM environment was successfully established for the remaining threat-detection and incident-response activities.
